7. Third-Party Material

The corpora under nl/ are redistributed under the terms their upstream
sources declare, listed in nl/README.md. DafnyBench is not redistributed
here. The packages tup builds from, and the software inside a built image,
carry their own licenses, recorded in the receipts. The seven verifiers are
separate programs under their own licenses and are not part of the Work.

8. Provenance

SHA256SUMS lists a hash for every file of the Work at the version it names,
and SHA256SUMS.sig is a signature over that list made with the copyright
holder's key (verify with ssh-keygen -Y verify, see NOTICE). They record what
this repository contained and when, so a copy can be compared against it.

9. Commercial license

A commercial license, including use in a product, a service, a deployment or
model training outside Research Use, is available from the copyright holder.
The contact is in NOTICE.

